From 0c5595bce9056d16f478f63e8d4c4a347d07c800 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:18:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sign: add the vendor mechanism CKM_TPM2_CERTIFY

TPM2_Certify of a key object, signed by a persistent TPM key the caller
names, through C_SignInit/C_Sign. A client holding the signer's public
key verifies, without trusting the module, that a PKCS#11 object is a key
of that TPM: the statement carries the nonce the client sent, and the
object's Name, which the client computes from CKA_TPM2_PUB_BLOB.

The module's logged-in session already holds what TPM2_Certify needs (the
loaded object and its unwrapped auth), so nothing secret leaves the
module. CKA_SIGN and CKA_ALLOWED_MECHANISMS are not consulted: the
mechanism signs nothing the key holder chose, and it certifies keys that
can sign nothing (decrypt-only, AES, HMAC).

Add src/tpm2-pkcs11-vendor.h, installed, which fixes the numbers of
CKA_TPM2_PUB_BLOB and CKM_TPM2_CERTIFY and the parameter layout. The
other CKA_TPM2_* attributes stay unstable and undocumented.

Test: pkcs-certify.int certifies EC, RSA, AES and HMAC keys, one needing a
context login, verifies the signature with OpenSSL, and checks the
refusals. docs/VENDOR.md describes the interface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
